# A thing worked down is BROKEN, not shrunk (owner, 2026-09-17; Broken): the same
# boulder with a piece off it, standing as wide as it ever did, cut flat where the
# pick went and pale there, because nothing has settled on a face opened a minute
# ago. That last part is the whole point of the change, so it is shown in the two
# lands whose ground weathers a rock least alike: the bog and the salt.
#
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/broken.tour --seed=4 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --give=pick:1 --held=pick
#
# Seed 4 because it is a seed whose bog AND salt each hold a boulder; seed 1's bog
# has none, and `near` would walk out of the land the frame is named after. The
# camera is low, because what is being shown is one face of one rock.
zoom 5
# A boulder in the bog, whole: the wear of a wet land all over it.
place moss
near boulder
wait 0.8
shot 01-a-boulder-in-the-bog-whole with prop:boulder,land:moss
# One go with the pick takes half of it. What is left stands where it stood, as
# wide as it was, with a flat pale face on top.
press use 0.1
await took 20
wait 0.8
shot 02-half-of-it-off-and-the-cut-unweathered with worked_down,prop:boulder,land:moss
# The same cut on the salt, where the ground bleaches everything standing in it
# and the fresh face is still the palest thing on the rock.
place salt_flats
near boulder
wait 0.8
shot 03-a-boulder-on-the-salt-whole with prop:boulder,land:salt_flats
press use 0.1
await took 20
wait 0.8
shot 04-cut-open-on-the-salt with worked_down,prop:boulder,land:salt_flats
# The last go takes it away: a worked thing is never left as a pebble.
press use 0.1
await took 20
wait 1.2
shot 05-the-last-go-takes-it-away
